{
  "id": 388036871,
  "iid": 20058,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "btatt: Make ATT dissector bearer-aware",
  "description": "Currently, the BT ATT dissector assumes that all PDUs are sent over the same single bearer. There is no accounting for multiple concurrent bearers -- e.g. GATT-over-BR/EDR or EATT bearers -- which goes against the ATT spec:\n\n> An Attribute protocol request and response or indication-confirmation pair is considered a single transaction. A transaction shall always be performed on one ATT bearer, and shall not be split over multiple ATT bearers.\n\nThis (for instance) means that when 2 ATT Requests are sent back-to-back on different bearers for different handles, the ATT dissector incorrectly interprets their Responses as being for the *same* handle.\n\nBelow are 2 ATT Requests for handles 0x16 and 0x18, but their Responses are decoded as both being for handle 0x18, which makes no sense: \n\n![image](/uploads/5101e0e9b63e9a03c8e16ff6d91a54f1/image.png){width=1288 height=165}\n\nTherefore, when tracking transactions, the bearer CID should be used as an extra key to ensure uniqueness in the record-keeping.\n\nAfter applying these proposed changes, the Responses are now decoded correctly for each handle:\n\n![image](/uploads/12dde66a7704441dbfb7193f770130a8/image.png){width=1288 height=165}\n\nThe sample HCI snoop is attached: [bearer_error_mini.snoop](/uploads/374a038859238fdd7ea35153f642b721/bearer_error_mini.snoop)",
  "state": "merged",
